 "problems": [
  "Each row prints five monetary pairs (monthly/annual) in order: Est. Common Charges without Contribution, Est. Real Estate Taxes First Year, Est. Real Estate Taxes Second Year, Est. Carrying Costs without Contribution, Est. Common Charges with Contribution. I mapped cc_m/cc_a to the first (\"without Contribution\") pair, tax_m/tax_a to the \"First Year\" pair, tax2_m to the Second Year monthly figure, and carry_m to the Carrying Costs monthly figure; the \"with Contribution\" common charges pair (last two columns) is not captured by the requested schema and was omitted.",
  "The table has no \"half bath\" or decimal bath column; Baths values are single whole numbers so all rows were read as full_baths with half_baths 0.",
  "The Ltd. Common Element letter codes (T=Terrace, B=Balcony) are present for some units in ext_sf's adjacent column but ext_sf itself was not printed as a separate numeric column from int_sf/gross; the \"Uninhabitable Ltd. Common Element Approx. Area sq. ft.\" figures (122, 80, 313, 245, 157, 71, 228, etc.) were placed in sf2 since they represent a second, uninhabitable area column, not placed in ext_sf since no distinct outdoor-area number was printed separately from this.",
  "Total row's full_baths/half_baths/beds totals were not printed as single figures; only building totals for area, price, percent, common charges (without), and real estate taxes (first year) were printed, so those unprinted total fields are \"-\".",
  "outdoor space left out: its column did not add up to the printed total"
 ],
